# A session finishes a turn while the user is away from its pane. Telegram gets a
# message headed by the session's name with what the session last said. The user
# replies to it on the phone; the reply is typed into the session and sent, and the
# phone sees a thumbs-up on its message.

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_gh
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

# What the real Copilot would have persisted as its last message, then a turn that
# ends while we are back at the list: that is what makes it an attention event.
# Copilot writes Markdown; the phone gets it as Telegram formatting, not as asterisks.
# A `#12` in the prose becomes a link into the project's repository, which the fake gh
# names; the same number inside code is left as it is.
type e2e:work 1500 Finished the **refactor** for #12 and the tests pass. Run `cargo test #12` to see. Shall I open the PR?
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session

telegram_wait message: <b>(Existing app session)</b>
telegram_expect_not Ready for attention
telegram_wait Finished the <b>refactor</b> for <a href="https://github.com/o/r/issues/12">#12</a> and the tests pass. Run <code>cargo test #12</code> to see.
telegram_expect_not **refactor**
telegram_dump 01-notified
dump 01-list-after-turn

telegram_say Yes, open it and request a review
wait 4000
telegram_dump 02-after-say
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling
wait_for Fake Copilot received: Yes, open it and request a review
telegram_wait reaction on
telegram_expect_not Not delivered
dump 02-reply-delivered
telegram_dump 02-reply-delivered
